   "parameter": "y is the positive real root of y^3+y^2+y=1; R is the native square-face radius, alpha^2/sqrt(2+2alpha^2) with alpha=1/y",
   "classical_basis_rows_native": "2R * [[1,0,1/2],[0,0,1/y-1],[0,1,-1/2]]",
   "source_proof": "After division by R, each canonical snub cube lies in C={|x_i|<=1, sum|x_i|<=1+y+y^2}. A lattice difference is (2a+l,2(y+y^2)l,2b-l). For |l|>=2, its middle coordinate exceeds 2. For l=0 a nonzero difference has an outer coordinate at least 2. For |l|=1 the outer coordinates are odd: if either has magnitude >=3 a coordinate separates; otherwise the L1 norm equals 2(1+y+y^2). Thus the whole C cells, and hence all snub cubes, have disjoint interiors for every nonzero integer word.",
